# Newsletter Sign-Up Form

Here's a complete, accessible newsletter sign-up form you can drop into your site. I'll give you a few variations depending on your setup.

## Option 1: Standalone HTML + CSS + JS (No dependencies)

```html
<section class="newsletter" aria-labelledby="newsletter-heading">
  <div class="newsletter__inner">
    <h2 id="newsletter-heading">Stay in the loop</h2>
    <p>Get product updates and tips delivered to your inbox. No spam, unsubscribe anytime.</p>

    <form
      id="newsletter-form"
      class="newsletter__form"
      action="/api/subscribe"
      method="POST"
      novalidate
    >
      <label for="newsletter-email" class="visually-hidden">Email address</label>
      <input
        type="email"
        id="newsletter-email"
        name="email"
        placeholder="you@example.com"
        autocomplete="email"
        required
        aria-describedby="newsletter-status"
      />
      <!-- honeypot for bots -->
      <input type="text" name="company" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" class="hp" aria-hidden="true" />
      <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
    </form>

    <p id="newsletter-status" class="newsletter__status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .newsletter { padding: 3rem 1.5rem; background: #f7f7f8; }
  .newsletter__inner { max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; }
  .newsletter__inner h2 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.75rem; }
  .newsletter__inner p { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; color: #555; }

  .newsletter__form { display: flex; gap: .5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; }
  .newsletter__form input[type="email"] {
    flex: 1 1 260px;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: .75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .newsletter__form input[type="email"]:focus {
    outline: 2px solid #2563eb;
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-color: #2563eb;
  }
  .newsletter__form button {
    padding: .75rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #fff;
    background: #2563eb;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .newsletter__form button:hover { background: #1d4ed8; }
  .newsletter__form button:disabled { opacity: .6; cursor: not-allowed; }

  .newsletter__status { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: .95rem; min-height: 1.25rem; }
  .newsletter__status.is-error { color: #b91c1c; }
  .newsletter__status.is-success { color: #047857; }

  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; }
  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px;
    padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0;
  }
</style>

<script>
  (function () {
    const form = document.getElementById('newsletter-form');
    const status = document.getElementById('newsletter-status');
    const button = form.querySelector('button');

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();

      const email = form.email.value.trim();
      if (!email || !/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)) {
        status.textContent = 'Please enter a valid email address.';
        status.className = 'newsletter__status is-error';
        return;
      }
      if (form.company.value) return; // bot filled honeypot

      button.disabled = true;
      status.textContent = 'Subscribing…';
      status.className = 'newsletter__status';

      try {
        const res = await fetch(form.action, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Accept: 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({ email }),
        });
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);

        status.textContent = 'Thanks! Check your inbox to confirm your subscription.';
        status.className = 'newsletter__status is-success';
        form.reset();
      } catch (err) {
        status.textContent = 'Something went wrong. Please try again.';
        status.className = 'newsletter__status is-error';
      } finally {
        button.disabled = false;
      }
    });
  })();
</script>
```

## Option 2: React component

```jsx
import { useState } from "react";

export default function NewsletterForm({ endpoint = "/api/subscribe" }) {
  const [email, setEmail] = useState("");
  const [status, setStatus] = useState({ state: "idle", message: "" });

  async function handleSubmit(e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    if (!/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)) {
      return setStatus({ state: "error", message: "Please enter a valid email." });
    }
    setStatus({ state: "loading", message: "Subscribing…" });
    try {
      const res = await fetch(endpoint, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: JSON.stringify({ email }),
      });
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error();
      setStatus({ state: "success", message: "Thanks! Check your inbox to confirm." });
      setEmail("");
    } catch {
      setStatus({ state: "error", message: "Something went wrong. Try again." });
    }
  }

  return (
    <section className="newsletter">
      <h2>Stay in the loop</h2>
      <p>Get updates delivered to your inbox.</p>
      <form onSubmit={handleSubmit} className="newsletter__form" noValidate>
        <label htmlFor="nl-email" className="visually-hidden">Email</label>
        <input
          id="nl-email"
          type="email"
          value={email}
          onChange={(e) => setEmail(e.target.value)}
          placeholder="you@example.com"
          autoComplete="email"
          required
        />
        <button type="submit" disabled={status.state === "loading"}>
          {status.state === "loading" ? "Subscribing…" : "Subscribe"}
        </button>
      </form>
      <p role="status" aria-live="polite" className={`status ${status.state}`}>
        {status.message}
      </p>
    </section>
  );
}
```

## Wiring it to a backend

The form posts JSON `{ "email": "..." }` to `/api/subscribe`. Pick one of these:

**Option A: Use a hosted service (easiest)**
- **Buttondown, ConvertKit, Mailchimp, Resend, MailerLite** — most offer a direct form action or simple API. Example with Mailchimp (no JS needed):
  ```html
  <form action="https://YOURUSER.us1.list-manage.com/subscribe/post?u=XXX&id=YYY" method="POST" target="_blank">
  ```
- **Formspree / Basin** — just change `action` to their endpoint, no backend needed.

**Option B: Your own endpoint** (Node/Express example):

```js
app.post("/api/subscribe", async (req, res) => {
  const { email } = req.body || {};
  if (!email || !/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: "Invalid email" });
  }
  // Save to DB or forward to provider (Mailchimp, Resend, etc.)
  // e.g. await resend.contacts.create({ email, audienceId: "..." });
  res.json({ ok: true });
});
```

## Quick checklist before going live

- [ ] Update `action`/`endpoint` to your real subscribe URL
- [ ] Add a **double opt-in** confirmation email (GDPR-friendly)
- [ ] Add a link to your **privacy policy** near the form
- [ ] Add rate limiting on your endpoint to prevent abuse
- [ ] Test with keyboard only (Tab + Enter) — should work
- [ ] Verify the status message is announced by screen readers (it uses `role="status"`)

Want me to adapt this to a specific platform — WordPress, Webflow, Next.js, Astro, Squarespace, or a specific email provider like ConvertKit/Mailchimp? Just tell me your stack.

